Z||000012||Gokart||07-30-2000||07:43 AM||||I saved the way Carolles applied his when he mailed me back with my questions(THANKS!), but let me post EXACTLY what the man himself says when I get the stuff. Should be here early this week!<P>Marc 87GT||||reg||1
Z||000013||Carrolles||07-31-2000||01:47 PM||||Sorry ofr the delay in replying, I've had company in town for a few days and they were staying in the spare room with the computer.<P>I just used a piece of vacuum tubing connected to one of the vacuum ports on the intake plenum.  Dip the other end in the can of juice and it will suck it in as the engine runs.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000014||Bruce||07-31-2000||09:03 PM||||Did you notice a difference after the treatment?||||reg||1
Z||000015||Gokart||07-31-2000||09:45 PM||||Carrolles, got the kit today. One can says to add directly to fuel, one says to spray into throttle body and the other is a BG Fuel injection cleaner and says to only use BG supply tools and adapters following instructions provided with tool! When I shake the can I can hear something in there besides the liquid! Is this the stuff you vaccumed through the plenum? If not, how did you apply it? Thanks! <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||5
Z||000016||Gokart||08-01-2000||09:45 PM||||Here it is straight from Ed! "Marc, sorry for the delayed response, still catching up after being at<BR>the Nationals for 4 days.<P>The fuel injector cleaner can now says "use apparatus" which a<BR>professional shop would have. It forces the cleaner into the fuel rail<BR>for faster (in garage) results. This can used to say "pour in tank", and<BR>that is how we can still use it.<P>Both injector and carbon dissolver are for 20 gals, so use 1/2 can for a<BR>full Fiero tank. They can be used at the same time, but don't use a full<BR>can in a Fiero tank. I would use these in 2 successive full tanks.<P>The oil disolver is sprayed into the throttle body with the engine<BR>running. Make sure you get some in the IAC air passage or first remove<BR>the IAC and spray a little on it (don't push on the pintle) and into the<BR>air passage. Then replace the IAC and start the engine. You will need to<BR>give the engine enough throttle to keep it running, while spraying. Same<BR>way on 4 cyl Fiero's.<P>Just heard from a Fiero friend out west that found the kit at a dealer<BR>and needed the fuel injector apparatus explained, so if you don't mind,<BR>will post to the list for others to know they can put it in the tank, if<BR>they find it elsewhere.<P>Glad to have helped before, and hope you feel the $40 + $6 s&h is worth<BR>it.<P>If you don't, The Fiero Factory will refund your $, but think you will<BR>thank your wife for ordering the kit.<P>We do. Thanks."<P><BR>||||reg||14
